        "id": 114597,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-27T14:39:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think KNYFE and Choke were close. Very close, once upon a time. Maybe they were both on the Special Operations unit and went on countless missions together during KNYFEs decade+ in FILTER, a large measure of trust was built between them. It's hard to get close to people when you are an agent of FILTER, but there was probably a great deal of compfort in that relationship.</p><p>It must have felt like the worst kind of betrayal when KNYFE went rogue. And Choke knows full well how betrayal is repaid in FILTER.</p><p>That's my guess. The psychic damage is that mental toll it takes on you to kill someone you once considered your closest friend.</p>",
